The National Vulnerability Database
-----------------------------------

src/nist_nvd/schema/*.yaml, src/nist_nvd/datamodel/ and project/ model the
JSON responses of the NVD API 2.0, as the National Institute of Standards
and Technology (NIST) publishes their JSON schemas at
https://csrc.nist.gov/schema/nvd/api/2.0/. They are this project's
rendering, in its own words. They are not NIST's, and their use does not
imply endorsement or certification by NIST or the NVD.

upstream/ holds copies of those JSON schemas, and tests/data/nvd/ holds a
small extract of the API's responses, each unchanged. NIST's statement on
its data and works
(https://www.nist.gov/open/copyright-fair-use-and-licensing-statements-srd-data-software-and-technical-series-publications,
read on 2026-11-03) asks a distribution to carry this statement:

  This data/work was created by employees of the National Institute of
  Standards and Technology (NIST), an agency of the Federal Government.
  Pursuant to title 17 United States Code Section 105, works of NIST
  employees are not subject to copyright protection in the United States.
  This data/work may be subject to foreign copyright. The data/work is
  provided by NIST as a public service and is expressly provided "AS IS."
  NIST MAKES NO WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS, IMPLIED OR STATUTORY,
  INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, THE IMPLIED WARRANTY OF MERCHANTABILITY,
  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, NON-INFRINGEMENT AND DATA ACCURACY.
  NIST does not warrant or make any representations regarding the use of
  the data or the results thereof, including but not limited to the
  correctness, accuracy, reliability or usefulness of the data.

The statement goes on to release NIST from liability; its address above
gives the rest. The records in the extract republish text that others wrote:
the CVE Program's records, and the Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog of
the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA).

NIST's SSVC schema
------------------

upstream/ssvc-v2.0.3.structure.json is NIST's
https://csrc.nist.gov/schema/nvd/api/2.0/ssvc-v2.0.3.json with every
description and example removed, which leaves its keys, types and
requirements. NIST's file states no licence, and its subject is the
Stakeholder-Specific Vulnerability Categorization of the CERT Coordination
Center, whose repository (https://github.com/CERTCC/SSVC) places its material
under other terms. This project cannot tell who wrote the descriptions, so it
copies none of them. The watch holds the structure to NIST's published file.

The Forum of Incident Response and Security Teams
-------------------------------------------------

upstream/external/cvss-v*.json are NIST's copies of the CVSS JSON schemas of
the Forum of Incident Response and Security Teams (FIRST.Org, Inc.), each
unchanged and each carrying FIRST's copyright notice and BSD-style licence
inside the file. Neither FIRST nor NIST endorses this project.

